Omarchy 4.0.4's audio scripts parse pactl's text and JSON output, which pactl
translates in a localized session (zh_TW, zh_CN, ko_KR): "Sink Input #",
"Name:", "Ports:", "not available", "Mute: yes" no longer match, so output
switching, the output list and the volume OSD fail there. Run only the parsed
pactl calls in the C locale (Omarchy itself does this for `pacman -Qi`); the
rest of each script keeps the session's language. Reported upstream; remove
once the pinned Omarchy parses pactl in the C locale.

--- a/bin/omarchy-audio-output-set-default
+++ b/bin/omarchy-audio-output-set-default
@@ -19,7 +19,8 @@
 # sink input but carries no application.name, and moving it would rewire the
 # processing itself -- onto headphones, or into its own virtual sink, which is a
 # cycle. EasyEffects' output stream must stay put for the same reason.
-timeout 2 pactl list sink-inputs 2>/dev/null | awk '
+# pactl translates its headers; parse them in the C locale.
+LC_ALL=C timeout 2 pactl list sink-inputs 2>/dev/null | awk '
   /^Sink Input #/ {id = substr($3, 2)}
   /application\.name = / {
     app = $0
--- a/bin/omarchy-audio-output-sink
+++ b/bin/omarchy-audio-output-sink
@@ -27,7 +27,8 @@
 
 # A DSP sink feeds its physical output through a stream of its own; follow that
 # stream down to the sink underneath.
-downstream="$(pactl list sink-inputs 2>/dev/null |
+# pactl translates its headers; parse them in the C locale.
+downstream="$(LC_ALL=C pactl list sink-inputs 2>/dev/null |
   awk -v virt="$sink" '
     /^Sink Input #/ {target = ""}
     /^[[:space:]]*Sink:/ {target = $2}
